# router_yuan_seedtrim.py - router_yuan_cov.py plus a seed-purchase cap.
# 2026-09-05.
#
# WHY. Three replays against 2,745-2,787-rated opponents were byte-identical
# mirrors of our own tape that we lost by 665, 298 and 666 on banks of 117k,
# 45k and 119k. In ep 103993606 the entire loss is one order: at step 265 we
# buy BUY_SEED STRAWBERRY 23, they buy 17. The $600 gap opens there and never
# closes; the final margin is -665. We end the season holding 6 STRAWBERRY
# seeds, they end holding none.
#
# Seed left in the shed at turn 720 scores nothing and cannot be sold back.
# Across all 65 tapes, 36 buy seed they never plant: $390 a season on average,
# $1,110 at worst, 247 surplus STRAWBERRY units in total.
#
# WORTH. Over 813 rated ladder episodes the margin distribution is dense at
# zero (median +832, IQR -3,037..+6,860), so a universal edge this size flips
# real games: +$500 flips 33 of 813, +$1,000 flips 62 (+7.6 win-rate points).
# The ladder pays for wins, not margin.
#
# WHAT. _trim_seed_buys caps every BUY_SEED at what the selected tape still
# plants, minus what the shed already holds. Nothing else differs from
# router_yuan_cov.py: same tapes, same routing, same sell-advance rim.
